-- =====================================================================
-- Shared fixture for the pool / Radar equivalence tests (859, 880).
--
-- Included with \ir AFTER _shared/fixtures.psql, inside the caller's
-- transaction (every row is rolled back with it). It reaches every gate
-- code the pool has, both waves, every booking state the readers branch
-- on, a two-day job with the same staff on both days, the 2 h gap at
-- another venue and back-to-back at the same one, the term cap and the
-- escalation radius. It leaves psql variables for every row and three
-- tables: t854_sec (the sections), t854_staff (the workers asked about one
-- at a time) and t854_users (the staff users Radar is read as).
--
-- Moved out of 859 unchanged (20261021130000) so 880 compares the next
-- bodies over the same rows. The .psql extension keeps pg_prove from
-- running it as a test.
-- =====================================================================
-- =====================================================================
-- The fixture: one row for every gate, both waves, every booking state
-- the readers branch on. Wednesday of the week two weeks ahead is "the
-- day"; s1 is the section most things are measured against.
-- =====================================================================
select cap_week_start(current_date) + 14 as w \gset

\set role2  '85430000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'
\set ve2    '85430000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002'
\set ve3    '85430000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003'
\set ser    '85430000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004'

